The review report has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/cross-cutting/xcut-04-enduse-string-consistency.md`.

**Summary of findings**: 8 findings (2 high, 3 medium, 3 low). The key issues:

1. **High**: Metrics aggregates end-use energy by equipment name, not `EndUse` category — multiple `HVAC_HEATING` devices produce separate line items
2. **High**: Missing HPXML end-use categories (cooking, laundry, dishwasher, pool pump, spa, ceiling fan) all collapsed into `OTHER`/`VENTILATION`
3. **Medium**: `EndUse` strings use snake_case (`"hvac_heating"`) vs HPXML convention (`"Heating"`)
4. **Medium**: `PortContribution` has no end-use field, preventing per-end-use port-level traceability
5. **Medium**: `IdealHvac` dynamically mutates `descriptor.end_use` mid-timestep (race condition)
6-8. **Low**: No centralized enum validation, no typo protection, case-sensitive string aggregation
